# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc asinh. For an exact real x the exact path returns ln(x+sqrt(x^2+1)), which is ln(1+x+O(x^2)): its evalf at Digits cancels -log10|x| digits (asinh(1/10^100) at Digits 40 = -5.9e-39, at Digits 12 = -1.4e-14), so a sign decided on it takes the noise: surd(asinh(1/10^100),3) gave -(-asinh(...))^(1/3), the complex root of a negative number (-2.32e-34-4.02e-34*i, right 4.64158883361e-34), the same for 10^-200, 3*10^-300, 10^-300, and evalf(asinh(10^-400)) at Digits 12 was 3e-78 (right 1e-400). Now asinh of an exact real below 1/4 in size (its double; a double that reads 0 too) stays unevaluated, as an exact complex one below 1/4 does since patch 0020 (G133), and evalf takes the MPFR asinh. A float x, a free x and |x| >= 1/4 keep the form (CAS asinh(-1/2) = ln(-1/2+sqrt((-1/2)^2+1)), asinh(-2) = -ln(2+sqrt((-2)^2+1))).
